{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/483333-pacts-effects","id":483333,"title":"Pacts effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-17T01:09:57-07:00","id":483333,"title":"Pacts effects","content":"Hey everyone, i searched this topic in the forum and could only find this (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/239545-initiation-of-pacts\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ation-of-pacts</a>) which doesnt really answer what i am thinking:<br /> <br /> which is a 2 part question:<br /> Lets say i have someone in my life who doesnt like me, that i have some sort if rivalry/ a person that hates me (to which i am object of that hate), could i trade that relationship to a demon? (Or i cant sell relations to which i am object? - which would beg me the question, if i were famous and got tired of it i could sell my &quot;fame&quot; to a demon?), or being quite direct: can i sell someone who doesnt like me (even if i dont have bad feelings about) out of my life?<br /> <br /> Part 2<br /> <br /> If lets say i sold my enemy or my fame to a demon, am I instantly anonymous and free of the hate of my enemy? Or the demon has to cash in the pact, effect that into a patchjob before i can feel the effect?<br /> <br /> And if its not necessary for this relation to be added ti a cover, although the fame in itself is not a problem, what happens to the hate of my ex-enemy? Is it still there just waiting for a face? He knows he hates someone but cant remember who?<br /> <br /> <br /> Any insights on these questions will be much appreciated","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T04:30:04-07:00","id":483407,"title":"","content":"The enemy I'd say would be worth (2) and yes if you traded that away you would no longer be the focus of the hate. The cover they integrated this relationship would become the focus of this (or any demon it is later traded to). All memories associated with you are now associated to the demon but your enemies friends are unaffected. <br /> <br /> The fame is harder for me to say 1) it is not a direct relationship but 2) it could be integrated into a pact potentially but risky. Only those directly effected would be altered so the fans but not their friends and family. The papers may be affected but what about bloggers and distanced news sources? Also people research famous people alot, taking on the fame could lead to the cover unravelling because things don't add up or just fans being fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T20:55:28-07:00","id":484219,"title":"","content":"I agree with Mr. FIX in regards to both points. Specifically, the concept of fame that you would be selling to the demon would be something that could be done, but most likely not something that would practically done for an extended period of time or thought to be a long term contract, in my opinion, because essentially too many independent entities are affected by the transfer of the fame, and while the deal is conceivable and doable, it would cause a lot of Compromise rolls when people randomly looked up the famous person on the internet. While general information could be changed or not cause issue, detailed and sourced wikipedia pages and the like, for example, would cause some issue....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5032-jackofshadows","name":"Jackofshadows","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T12:40:54-07:00","id":485576,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers, but there is still one question: When does it take starting to effect? If you trade the fame or enemy, does the mortal that made the trade only have the benefits after the demon adds that part to a cover?<br /> And if not, taking again the example of the enemy, where does his hate is directed to until that relation is added to a cover? <br /> <br /> Actually, outside this 2 examples, what happens to any relation that is not immediately added to a cover - or that option is not possible? As soon as the pact if firmed, it adds to a demon cover (automatically to the one he is currently using in case he does not have more?). So if you get a girlfriend, or as I recall from an example here &quot;playing tennis with boss&quot; from someone else, can you put that on hold unlimited? for sometime until you find the right patchwork?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T03:27:06-07:00","id":506590,"title":"","content":"Yep i wanted to know this too, it hapened on my game too, I ruled that the piece of Cover(a child taken from a mother who was using while posing as social service workers) was &quot;living on the street until cashed, but it was kinda awkward...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5064-clonea85m09","name":"Clonea85m09","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T06:03:47-07:00","id":506686,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would say that trading the fame is easily doable on a long term basis. It just would rewrite the world so that everything that the famed character did, the demon who clames the fame did. All the TV shows, all the media, etc. You might lose a good portion of your family and friends as well to the deal, depending on how much is tied up into the idea of your fame. <br /> <br /> <br /> Patchworks generally take effect immediately, unless you're using the Promissory rules in the Interface book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}